     1	<img src="website/static/img/ProveNFix.png" alt="logo" width="15%" />
     2	
     3	# ProveNFix 
     4	
     5	ProveNFix is a program analysis and repair tool for temporal properties for C language. 
     6	ProveNFix is written in [OCaml](https://ocaml.org/), and built on top of the Meta [Infer](http://fbinfer.com/) tool. 
     7	
     8	[Infer](http://fbinfer.com/) ![build](https://github.com/facebook/infer/actions/workflows/install.yml/badge.svg) ![website](https://github.com/facebook/infer/actions/workflows/deploy.yml/badge.svg) is a static analysis tool for Java,
     9	C++, Objective-C, and C. Infer is written in [OCaml](https://ocaml.org/). 
    10	Read Infer's [Getting
    11	Started](http://fbinfer.com/docs/getting-started) page for
    12	details on how to install packaged versions of Infer. 
    13	
    14	
    15	
    16	The repository provides the artifact for the FSE24 paper: **ProveNFix: Temporal Property guided Program Repair**. 
    17	Our [Benchmarks](https://zenodo.org/records/10695186) are available from Zenodo.
    18	The [Source Code](https://github.com/songyahui/infer_TempFix) of the tool is available from GitHub. 
    19	The final version of the [Paper](ProveNFix_Paper.pdf) and the [Appendix](ProveNFix_Appendix.pdf) are publicly accessible. 
    20	
    21	
    22	## Build ProveNFix
    23	
    24	We have a docker image to try out our tool, which is detailed in the [Artifact Evaluation Doc](ProveNFix_Artifact_Evaluation.pdf). 
    25	```
    26	docker pull yahuuuuui/fse24-prove_n_fix:ubuntu
    27	docker run -i -t yahuuuuui/fse24-prove_n_fix:ubuntu /bin/bash
    28	```
    29	The source code repository is placed in "/home/", called "infer_TempFix". 
    30	The benchmarks are also summarized in the docker env. 
    31	Alternatively, one could build \toolName from scratch using a Linux system (tested on Ubuntu 22.04.4 LTS), with the following dependencies: 
    32	
    33	```
    34	apt install menhir 
    35	apt install cmake 
    36	apt install z3 
    37	apt install sqlite3
    38	apt install opam 
    39	opam init
    40	opam switch create 4.14.0
    41	eval $(opam env)  
    42	git clone https://github.com/songyahui/infer_TempFix.git
    43	cd infer_TempFix
    44	./compile
    45	```
    46	
    47	## Run ProveNFix on the projects in experiments 1 and 2
    48	### Step 1: Put the default spec in the file ["spec.c"](./spec.c).
    49	 
    50	### Step 2: Run ProveNFix
    51	```
    52	../../git/infer_TempFix/infer/bin/tempFix
    53	``` 
    54	
    55	### Step 3: Check out the analysis/repair results in the file ["TempFix-out/detail.txt"](./TempFix-out/detail.txt)
    56	
    57	Here lists the pre-required commands for the benchmark projects
    58	
    59	### [Swoole](https://github.com/swoole/swoole-src)
    60	```
    61	phpize
    62	./configure
    63	```
    64	
    65	
    66	###  [lxc](https://github.com/lxc/lxc), [WavPack](https://github.com/dbry/WavPack), [p11-kit](https://github.com/p11-glue/p11-kit), [flex](https://github.com/westes/flex), [x264](https://github.com/mirror/x264), [recutils-1.8](https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/recutils/), [inetutils-1.9.4](https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/inetutils/), [snort-2.9.13](https://www.snort.org/downloads#), [grub](https://github.com/rhboot/grub2)
    67	```
    68	./autogen.sh 
    69	./configure
    70	```
    71	
    72	## Experiment 3: Automatically detect double free errors
    73	
    74	
    75	### Step1: Checkout the ProveNFix branch and re-build
    76	```
    77	git checkout doubleFreeClose
    78	./compile
    79	```
    80	
    81	### Step 2: Put the default spec (["spec_Temp_grub.c"](./spec_Temp_grub.c), ["spec_Temp_lxc.c"](./spec_Temp_lxc.c), ["spec_Temp_p11.c"](./spec_Temp_p11.c)) in the file ["spec.c"](./spec.c), and run ProveNFix on the projects Grub, lex, and p11-kit respectively. 
    82	 
    83	```
    84	../../git/infer_TempFix/infer/bin/tempFix
    85	``` 
    86	
    87	### Step 3: Check out the analysis/repair results in the file ["TempFix-out/detail.txt"](./TempFix-out/detail.txt)
    88	
    89	
    90	
    91	
    92	## Experiment 4: generating specs for the OpenSSL project
    93	
    94	### Step1: Checkout the ProveNFix branch and re-build
    95	```
    96	git checkout Infer_OpenSSL
    97	./compile
    98	```
    99	
   100	### Get the source code and unzip [OpenSSL](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/tag/openssl-3.1.2)
   101	```
   102	cd openssl-3.1.2
   103	./Configure --prefix=/usr/local/ssl --openssldir=/usr/local/ssl \
   104	    '-Wl,-rpath,$(LIBRPATH)'
   105	```
   106	
   107	### Add the first two specs in the file ["spec.c"](./spec.c).
   108	```
   109	#define SW_CHANNEL_MIN_MEM (1024*64)
   110	
   111	/*@ return(arg):
   112	    Post (TRUE, return(arg))@*/
   113	
   114	/*@ ERR_new():
   115	    Post (TRUE, ERR_new())@*/
   116	```
   117	
   118	### Run the ProveNFix
   119	```
   120	../../git/infer_TempFix/infer/bin/tempFix
   121	```
